From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:50:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build the near-plane clipping test without Windows' min and
 max macros

The first Visual Studio build of 0005 stopped in Open77.ScreenClip.Tests with
C2589 ("illegal token on right side of '::'") wherever the test calls
std::min or std::max. The test draws the depth pass's fan, so it includes
ScreenDepthPass.hpp, which brings in d3d12.h on Windows and with it the
Windows headers' min and max macros. Open77.Client and the other tests that
include Windows headers define NOMINMAX (and WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN); this target
now does too.

Reproduced here by giving MinGW's d3d12.h the macros MSVC's headers define
(MinGW's own C++ library defines NOMINMAX itself, so it did not show it):
the test fails as on Windows without the definition and compiles with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SGDf5e3noD7RiVDkPCENkG
---
 client/CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/client/CMakeLists.txt b/client/CMakeLists.txt
index e013803..a069d12 100644
--- a/client/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/client/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1019,6 +1019,9 @@ if(BUILD_TESTING)
     # screen is in Open77.PerspectiveImage.Tests.
     add_executable(Open77.ScreenClip.Tests tests/ScreenClipTests.cpp)
     target_include_directories(Open77.ScreenClip.Tests PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src")
+    # It draws the depth pass's fan (ScreenDepthPass.hpp), whose header brings in
+    # d3d12.h and with it Windows' `min` and `max` macros on Windows.
+    target_compile_definitions(Open77.ScreenClip.Tests PRIVATE WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN NOMINMAX)
     set_target_properties(Open77.ScreenClip.Tests PROPERTIES FOLDER "Tests")
     add_test(NAME Open77.ScreenClip.Tests COMMAND Open77.ScreenClip.Tests)
 
